  "comments": "The standard weight of a half sovereign was 80/623 troy ounce (61.6 grains). The pure gold content was 56 312/623 grains (3.6612 g).<br /><br />\r\nNumerous obverse, reverse and overdate varieties exist (Spink lists 10). Between 1863 and 1880 gold coins issued by the Royal Mint for circulation in the UK and its possessions had a die number inscribed on the reverse under the wreath:<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM#735.1</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">without die number</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM#735.2</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">with die number</span><br /><br />\r\nNote: For issues with mintmark below the shield see <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/australia_colonial-1.html\">Australia</a> (M = Melbourne mint, S = Sydney mint).",
